<code>assert !c.isEmpty() => \forall int i; 0<=i && i<c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>

However, since the comment specifies the condition that the collection is not null and the list should be equal to the collection after all its elements have been added, we need to adjust the assert statement to reflect that the list's size should be equal to the collection's size and each element should match. Here is the corrected version:

<code>assert this.size() == c.size() && \forall int i; 0<=i && i<c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert c != null => this.containsAll(c) && this.size() == c.size();</code>
--------------------
<code>assert c != null => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>
--------------------
